														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4335880">
									

<p>After some consideration, I've come to like this. It's nice to see a class set for each part of the acronym. I especially like the hybrid examples which deals with all of my previous complaints.</p>
<p>A few nitpicks:</p>
<ul>
<li>I feel like &quot;Disruption&quot; blends into &quot;Risk&quot; near the end. Just because something has affected the entire world wouldn't necessarily mean the Foundation would &quot;declare war&quot; on it&#8212; in fact, at that point it'd probably be easier to deem it consensus reality.</li>
<li>If Disruption Class is supposed to be related to light, why is &quot;Vlam&quot; blue? Blue is predominantly either a very cold or very hot colour. Having it be the second-weakest of the bunch seems&#8230; out-of-place. I get that there's a colour scheme here but, well, it's just odd to my eye.</li>
</ul>
<p>Other than that: real good job on this you guys. This looks slick as hell.</p>

							</div>

								
					
