			<div class="content" id="post-content-4335942">
									

<blockquote>
<p>I feel like &quot;Disruption&quot; blends into &quot;Risk&quot; near the end. Just because something has affected the entire world wouldn't necessarily mean the Foundation would &quot;declare war&quot; on it— in fact, at that point it'd probably be easier to deem it consensus reality.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This is more related to the Anomaly's imminent destruction of the veil and/or normalcy. Essentially, that the anomaly's influence is so far reaching that it <em>is</em> threatening to become the norm. The idea is that the Foundation would find this far and away unacceptable and do everything in their power to stop it.</p>
<p>Really, this is only if The Foundation is aware that the anomaly has that sort of influence.</p>
<p>Of course, people are allowed to interpret that as they would like but I wanted to make sure Amida in particular was reserved for specific and dire situations.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>If Disruption Class is supposed to be related to light, why is &quot;Vlam&quot; blue?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Pretty much entirely for consistency's sake. I did initially consider making Disruption Class purely based around &quot;warm&quot; colors (Yellow -&gt; Red) but I ultimately decided that consistency was more important.</p>
<p>Thank you for the kind words as well!</p>

